# Pragmatic Testing

- Add or update tests for any meaningful behavior change.
- Prefer testing observable behavior over implementation details.
- Use simple fakes or fixtures first; avoid deep or brittle mocks.
- Mock only unstable boundaries (network, time, randomness, file IO, process env).
- For refactors, add regression tests before large moves when feasible.
- Keep tests easy to read: setup, execute, verify.
- Avoid over-asserting internal call counts unless behavior depends on it.

## Default test split

- `core/`: fast unit tests for pure transforms and wrapper contract shaping.
- `web/server/`: route/controller tests for request-response behavior.
- `web/client/`: tests around user-visible rendering logic when practical.

## Example

```js
// Prefer: mock fetch boundary, assert normalized response shape.
// Avoid: mocking every helper inside the same module under test.
```
